    {
      "at": "2026-09-22T19:47:13.627Z",
      "event": "ac-updated",
      "detail": "AC6 as frozen demanded that writes route through fs/write_text_file. apply_patch applies a multi-file diff atomically through git; the ACP write method writes one file's whole content with no diff semantics and no cross-file atomicity, so routing it would be a redesign, not a capability branch. AC6 now states what the design guarantees — reads route when advertised, writes and shell stay local with the reason recorded, and no absent capability is ever called — and the routing work is left to a follow-up flow."
    },
